+#+TITLE: /spec-report skill to report status of a spec
+
+artifact: a claude skill in this dir, and the report
+disable-model-invocation
+
+implementation note: because this skill produces its own =report.org=,
+do not commit a hand-made report. Use it to bootstrap the skill, but
+then remove it and apply the skill to produce the report.
+
+skill:
+- Read the spec file provided by args (=spec.org=, =SPEC.md=,
+  =spec--<name>.org=, =SPEC--<name>.md=)
+- Thoroughly analyze the working copy, to understand how well the repo
+  behavior implements the spec. Base this analysis on implementation
+  and documentation.
+- You can reference notes for context, but they are not part of the
+  spec implementation. Notes are typically things like =zib= files and
+  any text-only that isn't clearly part of the implementation, or
+  documenting the implementation.
+- Refer to commit history for additional context, evolution,
+  direction, and decisions made.
+- Produce a sibling report file (e.g. =report.org=, =REPORT.md=,
+  =report--<name>.org=, =REPORT--<name>.org=) corresponding to the
+  spec file
+  - report file name is produced by =s/^spec/report/ <spec>=
+  - indicate:
+    - concise summary status
+    - conflicts - any implemented behavior that contradicts the spec
+      - conflict resolution plan is a heading in the spec prefixed
+        with =conflict plan:=
+      - indicate whether or not spec includes a conflict resolution plan
+	for this specific conflict
+    - indicate any conflict resolution plans that can be removed from
+      spec, because the conflict has since been resolved
+    - what has not been implemented
+      - evaluate whether the spec and current implementation have enough
+	detail to produce a viable plan to implement it. If so, indicate
+	"ready to implement." If not, indicate "not ready to implement"
+	and provide a list of questions that user will need to answer in
+	the spec to support a plan.
+      - do not include the plan in the report - it is only a gap
+	analysis used identify necessary spec improvements.
+    - what has been implemented
+    - for all sections other than summary status, provide evidence
+      supporting the claims
+- commit the report, overwriting the existing report. The intent is to
+  refresh the report over time as the implementation changes. It
+  supports a spec-driven workflow, where the report describes how well
+  the implementation satisfies the spec.
+- in case of a sclr =report.org= (indicated by presence of a sibling
+  =lore.org=), move the sclr =report.org= to =sclr-report.org= in a
+  preparatory commit.
